   (e) use the Software for any commercial or business purpose;
   (f) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, or otherwise
       attempt to derive its source code, except to the extent that applicable
       law expressly prohibits such a restriction.

2. Public visibility is not a licence

   The source code of the Software may be viewable on a public code hosting
   platform. The mere fact that it can be viewed or downloaded does not
   constitute a licence or any transfer of rights. No rights of use are
   granted except those strictly required by the hosting platform's terms
